{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `counts`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += counts[c, k] * log(rule_prob[c, k])` likelihood with a single built-in `multinomial` sampling statement for the top-level protected count table. This is the normalized built-in count likelihood corresponding to the same categorical-count log probability. The Dirichlet prior on `rule_prob` was vectorized so the top-level parameter is sampled exactly once and not inside a loop. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Probabilistic Context-Free Grammar
data {
  int<lower=1> C;
  int<lower=1> K;
  array[C, K] int<lower=0> counts;
}
parameters {
  array[C] simplex[K] rule_prob;
}
model {
  rule_prob ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, K));
  counts ~ multinomial(rule_prob);
}
generated quantities {
  array[C] int<lower=1, upper=K> sampled_rule;
  for (c in 1:C) {
    sampled_rule[c] = categorical_rng(rule_prob[c]);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"C":4,"K":2,"counts":[[3,4],[3,4],[3,1],[4,3]]}","protected_variables":["counts"]}
